.git
.gitignore
**/__pycache__
**/*.pyc
.DS_Store
**/.DS_Store

# Notebooks and their outputs are development material, not part of the service.
# The glob matters as much as tutorials/: notebooks under src/ carry saved
# output cells that can hold participant records even where the data directory
# beside them is excluded below (match_performance_to_participant_v0.3.ipynb is
# 1.5 MB of them). Nothing in the service imports a notebook.
**/*.ipynb
**/.ipynb_checkpoints
tutorials/
UI/
tests/
tmp/
file_formats/
server_runs/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Raw human participant data -- must NOT enter the image.
#
# An image layer travels wherever the image goes: a registry, a teammate's
# laptop, the deploy host's disk. Anyone who can pull it can read every file in
# it, whether or not the API ever serves that file.
#
# assets/human_data/ is deliberately NOT listed here: it is the anonymised,
# consolidated output of assets/build_human_data.py (participants renumbered
# 1..N per study, every Prolific/session id stripped -- see its own README),
# and the pipeline genuinely reads it now
# (src/result_visualizer/study_comparisons.py, the human-vs-model report).
# Everything below this line is still raw and keyed by real participant or
# Prolific id, so it stays excluded.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

assets/human_trials_and_cognitive_parameters/

# Raw pre-anonymization sources (and the de-anonymization key itself) that
# live inside the otherwise-anonymized assets/human_data/ tree -- see
# .gitignore for why these specific files, and not the rest of the
# directory, are excluded.
assets/human_data/participant_id_map.csv
assets/human_data/CoAX/coax-3-datasets-user-responses.csv
assets/human_data/CoXAM/coxam-mushrooms-wine-quality-user-responses.csv
assets/human_data/CoXAM/overall_counterfactual_resultsv0.2.xlsx

# Per-participant fitted parameters and trial-by-trial records, keyed by
# Prolific participant id. The runner's FITTED_COAX_PARAMS holds the aggregate
# means it derives from these, so the source rows are not needed at runtime.
src/cognitive_models/CoAX/results/
src/cognitive_models/CoAX/data/
src/cognitive_models/CoXAM/datasets/
src/cognitive_models/CoXAM/outputs/

# The reference study's own UI and mockup server, not part of this service.
src/cognitive_models/CoAX/UI/
src/cognitive_models/CoAX/simulation_mockup/
